# {{ inventory_hostname }}: operations manual

Generated by Ansible (remote-exit-node). It contains WireGuard **private keys**: keep it in a
password manager only, never in git, email or chat. Re-run the playbook after any change
(e.g. after the box moves) to refresh it.

Not in this document, store separately: the **vault password**, the node user's **sudo
password**, the **SSH private key** (`{{ ansible_ssh_private_key_file | default('~/.ssh/...') }}`) and the repo's `.env`.

## 1. At a glance

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Node name | `{{ inventory_hostname }}` |
| Login user | `{{ ssh_user }}` |
| Hardware MAC ({{ node_wan_interface }}) | `{{ lan['macaddress'] }}` |
| LAN IP when generated | `{{ lan['address'] }}` |
| LAN gateway (router) when generated | `{{ lan['gateway'] }}` |
| Timezone | `{{ node_timezone }}` |
| Tailscale | {{ ('`' ~ tailscale_hostname ~ '` / `' ~ ts_ip ~ '`') if enable_tailscale | bool else 'disabled' }} |
| DuckDNS | {{ ('`' ~ duckdns_domain ~ '.duckdns.org`') if enable_duckdns | bool else 'disabled' }} |
| WireGuard endpoint | {{ ('`' ~ wireguard_endpoint ~ ':' ~ wireguard_port ~ '` (UDP)') if wg_on else 'disabled' }} |
| Node inside WireGuard | {{ ('`' ~ wireguard_ipv4_server ~ '`') if wg_on else 'n/a' }} |
| Heartbeat monitoring | {{ 'configured' if monitoring_heartbeat_url | length > 0 else 'not configured' }} |

## 2. How to log in

Two independent paths. If one is down, use the other.

**A. Tailscale (primary, works through any NAT)**

```bash
ssh {{ ssh_user }}@{{ tailscale_hostname }}
```

Tailscale SSH may ask you to confirm in a browser (re-checked every 12 h).

{% if wg_on %}
**B. WireGuard + SSH (backup, independent of Tailscale)**

1. Connect one of the WireGuard clients from section 5 (keep one, e.g. `{{ wireguard_peers[-1].name }}`, on your laptop as the emergency key).
2. Then:

```bash
ssh -i {{ ansible_ssh_private_key_file | default('~/.ssh/<key>') }} {{ ssh_user }}@{{ wireguard_ipv4_server }}
```

Needs section 3 in place. `{{ wireguard_ipv4_server }}` is fixed; it never changes.

{% endif %}
**C. Console**: a physical box: keyboard + monitor, log in as `{{ ssh_user }}` with the sudo
password. A cloud VM: the provider's serial/console connection (OCI: Instance → Console
connection) and Reboot from the instance page.

**Reach a device on the node's network** (e.g. a home router's admin page), from either path:

```bash
ssh -L 8080:{{ lan['gateway'] }}:80 {{ ssh_user }}@{{ tailscale_hostname if enable_tailscale | bool else wireguard_ipv4_server }}
# then open http://localhost:8080 (use :443 and https:// if the device requires it)
```

`{{ lan['gateway'] }}` is the node's gateway when this was generated (see `ip route` on the node).

No Tailscale subnet route is needed for this. The SSH tunnel uses the node as a hop only
while it is open, so its LAN is never exposed to your tailnet, nothing has to be approved in
the Tailscale console, and it also works over the WireGuard path. Same trick for any other
device: `ssh -L <local-port>:<device-ip>:<port> ...`.

## 3. Inbound access for WireGuard

{% if wg_on %}
Clients must reach **UDP {{ wireguard_port }}** on `{{ wireguard_endpoint }}`. Set up whichever applies:

| Where the node runs | What to configure |
|---|---|
| Behind a home router | DHCP reservation for MAC `{{ lan['macaddress'] }}` + port forward **UDP {{ wireguard_port }}** → that IP, port {{ wireguard_port }}. Nothing else: no TCP ports, no DMZ, no UPnP. |
| Cloud VM | Provider firewall ingress **UDP {{ wireguard_port }}** from `0.0.0.0/0` (OCI: security list or NSG). Optional: UDP 41641 for direct Tailscale connections. Remove TCP 22 once Tailscale SSH works. |

The node's own iptables rules {{ 'are integrated by the playbook (host_firewall: active on this node)' if iptables_on else 'need no changes on this node' }}.

Verify with `scripts/doctor.sh` from a different network (section 6). If UDP doesn't arrive
although the forward is set behind a home router: compare the router's WAN IP with
`curl -4 ifconfig.me` there. Different means CGNAT (WireGuard can't work) or a second router
in front (forward the port on both).
{% else %}
WireGuard is disabled: nothing to open or forward. For a physical box, a DHCP reservation for
MAC `{{ lan['macaddress'] }}` is still recommended.
{% endif %}

## 4. If something hangs

- **Physical box**: it starts by itself after a power cut. Whoever is on site: unplug the
  power, wait 10 seconds, plug it back in, wait 3 minutes. They shouldn't reset the router;
  a replaced router needs the section 3 setup again.
- **Cloud VM**: Reboot from the provider console. Always Free instances can be reclaimed when
  idle; a Pay As You Go account avoids that.
{% if not (monitoring_watchdog_dev.stat.exists | default(false)) %}
- This node has no hardware watchdog, so a hung system won't reboot by itself.
{% endif %}

