## 6. Health checks

From the repo on your laptop:

```bash
scripts/doctor.sh --env <this node's env file>   # node self-check{{ ' + UDP probe to the WireGuard endpoint' if wg_on else '' }}
```

On the node: `sudo exit-node-doctor`. The same node-side check runs with every heartbeat;
failures are reported to the heartbeat service's `/fail` endpoint. It does not prove traffic
through each tunnel: for that, ping `{{ wireguard_ipv4_server if wg_on else tailscale_hostname }}` through the tunnel from a
machine on your side (e.g. an uptime monitor).

IP forwarding is only switched on after the LAN guard rules are loaded. If the self-check
says "IPv4 forwarding off", exit traffic is stopped on purpose: run
`sudo systemctl start exit-node-lan-guard` and read its journal.

Acceptance tests (before shipping, and again on site):

| Test | Expected |
|---|---|
| `scripts/doctor.sh` from another network | No FAIL{{ '; probes reach the node' if wg_on else '' }} |
| Through each tunnel: `curl -4 ifconfig.me` | The node's public IP |
| Through each tunnel: `curl -6 ifconfig.me` | The node's IPv6 or failure, **never your own** |
| Through each tunnel: a device on the node's LAN (router admin page, ping), IPv4 and IPv6; on a cloud VM also `curl -m 5 http://169.254.169.254/` | Blocked (LAN guard) |
| https://dnsleaktest.com through each tunnel | Only resolvers at the node's location |
| Power cycle (physical box) or Reboot from the console (VM) | Both login paths back within ~3 min |
{% if wg_on and enable_duckdns | bool %}
| Remote WAN IP changes | DuckDNS follows within 5 min; note whether router clients recover alone |
{% endif %}

## 7. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Check |
|---|---|
| Tailscale shows the node offline | Power/network at its location, or the VM's state in the provider console (section 4). Try path B. |
| WireGuard stuck connecting | `scripts/doctor.sh` from outside: inbound UDP (section 3), DuckDNS, CGNAT / double NAT; toggle the client off/on |
| Pages stall over WireGuard | MTU: set `wireguard_mtu: 1380` and re-run the playbook |
| DuckDNS shows an old IP | `ssh ... 'systemctl status duckdns-update; journalctl -u duckdns-update -n 20'` |
| Everything down | Power cycle / console Reboot (section 4); if still down, it needs hands-on repair |

## 8. Maintenance (from the repo on your laptop)

```bash
ansible-playbook site.yml --limit {{ inventory_hostname }} --ask-vault-pass          # re-apply / refresh this manual
ansible-playbook site.yml --limit {{ inventory_hostname }} --ask-vault-pass --check --diff   # preview changes
EDITOR="code --wait" ansible-vault edit host_vars/{{ inventory_hostname }}/vault.yml     # change secrets
```

After the box moves, point `ansible_host` in `inventory.ini` at `{{ tailscale_hostname }}`.
Security updates install automatically; {{ ('kernel updates reboot the box at ' ~ baseline_unattended_reboot_time ~ ' local time.') if baseline_unattended_reboot | bool else 'reboot manually after kernel updates.' }}
